# Always open a PR and merge it to main

The owner's standing instruction (2026-11-05), for every request in this repo and
in its sibling repo (general_datebase / granite-webhooks):

1. Do the work on the session's branch, commit and push it.
2. Open a pull request into `main`.
3. Merge it into `main` once the repo's own checks for the change pass.

This does not need to be asked for again; the owner does not want to be asked.
It does not change the other rules: never run migrations, never touch the main
database, never deploy. Merging only lands code on `main`; deploys stay manual
(`workflow_dispatch`), so say which migrations must run before a deploy.
